    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Dj998i7jbCbdy2Z6GrciUq)_\n\n## What\n\n- Requested: inline keywords in Org text (for example in a draft for a project) show up in the agenda as problems to fix.\n- New agenda view `x`, \"Inline keywords to fix\", in `sp-agenda-views.el` (the owner of `org-agenda-custom-commands`, ADR 0009).\n- Also on `C-c o x` (`sp-agenda-views-inline`).\n- It uses Org's search view with a regexp, so each hit is an agenda entry with its context that jumps to the place on `RET`.\n\n## Settings\n\n- `sp-agenda-views-inline-keywords`: `FIXME`, `CITE`, `TK`, `XXX`; whole words only. Changing it re-installs the view.\n- `sp-agenda-views-inline-extra-dirs`: `sp-writing-projects`. Its Org files are scanned besides the agenda files, because draft headings are not always agenda entries.\n- The file title is shown as the prefix column (reuses `sp-agenda-views-file-title`).\n\n## Reading I chose\n\n- \"Inline\" means a keyword anywhere in an entry's heading or body, not an Org TODO keyword.\n- The agenda shows problems on demand in its own view; it is not added to the main PARA view or the morning list.\n\n## Not checked\n\n- No Emacs in the container: neither the code nor the new ERT test (`tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el`) was run.\n- Org's search view ignores text before a file's first heading.\n- Whether the search is case-insensitive depends on Org (so `fixme` may match).\n- Not added: a count in the dashboard or the morning view.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9jyyEFewgtDoWE5dF)_",
